From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 12:06:47 +0200
Subject: drm/msm/dp: serialize HPD plugged-state snapshot

HPD handlers update plugged while holding plugged_lock, but the IRQ
thread sampled it without synchronization. Take the same mutex around
the snapshot so transition filtering does not race with plug or unplug
handling.

Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -972,7 +972,9 @@ static irqreturn_t msm_dp_display_irq_thread(int irq, void *dev_id)
 	dp->hpd_isr_status = 0;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dp->irq_thread_lock, flags);
 
+	mutex_lock(&dp->plugged_lock);
 	was_plugged = dp->plugged;
+	mutex_unlock(&dp->plugged_lock);
 
 	/* notify only on actual state transitions */
 	if (hpd_isr_status & DP_DP_HPD_UNPLUG_INT_MASK && was_plugged)
-- 
